# Build context whitelist for the console-dashboard image.
#
# The context is the repository ROOT (the design library at ui/ has to be inside
# it), and the repository root is mostly a Go monorepo: app/, internal/, pkg/,
# deploy/, bus-bench/, plus test corpora. None of that belongs in a SvelteKit
# image's context, and sending it costs the build the time to hash and transfer
# every file. So this is a whitelist -- deny everything, re-admit by name --
# rather than the usual denylist, because a denylist would have to be edited
# every time the Go side grows a directory, and forgetting is silent.
#
# Per-image rather than one .containerignore at the root because the two console
# images want different trees (dashboard/ vs admin/) out of the same context.
# `buildah bud`/`podman build` take `--ignorefile <path>`, which is what makes
# two whitelists over one context possible; without it both images would share
# the root .containerignore and each would carry the other's sources.
#
# The `*` line excludes every top-level entry; each `!` line re-admits one path.
# Order matters: the last pattern a path matches decides, so the denials for
# generated directories come last.
*
!ui
!web/package.json
!web/bun.lock
!web/bunfig.toml
!web/tsconfig.base.json
!web/sorted-readdir.mjs
!web/serve-node.js
!web/kit
!web/dashboard

# The other three workspace members contribute their manifest and nothing else:
# `bun install --frozen-lockfile` re-resolves the whole workspace graph and
# fails ("lockfile had changes, but lockfile is frozen") if a member named in
# bun.lock has no package.json on disk. Their sources stay out; that is what
# keeps astro, sharp and mermaid off this image.
!web/admin/package.json
!web/marketing/package.json
!web/docs/package.json

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/build
**/.svelte-kit
**/.astro
**/test-results
**/*.log
